  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Ecclestone left school young, worked in a gasworks laboratory and built a successful motorcycle-parts dealership before moving from racing into management. He represented drivers, acquired the Brabham team and helped organise constructors through FOCA. That position allowed him to negotiate collectively, package television rights and centralise the commercial administration of Formula One.\n\nHis companies came to control broadcasting, promotion and race logistics, converting a loosely organised championship into a worldwide media property. Ecclestone remained the sport’s dominant commercial figure until Liberty Media took control in 2017. His achievements remain inseparable from hard bargaining and controversy; a later guilty plea for tax fraud resulted in a suspended prison sentence and a substantial settlement with British authorities.",
